u  think was happening to him were you all  able to communicate with each other  during that time what did you think  very little uh-huh very little so you  knew he was safe he was moved there were  just so many question marks what's  happening silence we're not told what's  going on what's going to happen I was  very isolated in prison I was four  some time in solitary confinement and  then in another prison that was quite  overcrowded and though I was accredited  like how well we were a cell for eight  people and had over 20 people there in  the self yes yes and there was very  little contact with the outside so I  could see no rain for example 35 minutes  a week through glass talking by phone  and so she actually is very strong and  had to take me through this emotionally  and spiritually she was the only one I  could receive truth from and so when she  would come in she would encourage me and  that's what would keep me going for the  next week Brunson much has been written  about about you and we followed your  your imprisonment for the past two years  do you believe you were a pawn and what  has been called hostage diplomacy that  the Turkish government held you as part  of an effort to exchange you for another  prisoner here well people have certainly  written that President Trump and also  senator Graham Lindsey Graham told me  that I just had the view from the cell  yeah and I think that even though  whatever reason the Turkish government  was holding us for I believe that God  was involved in this for us because I  think of millions of people who prayed  for Turkey during that time and how God  is bringing blessing out of it were they  interrogating you on a regular basis  were you beaten while you were in prison  how would you know I wasn't meeting the  problem is that I wasn't interrogated so  for the first 18 months I didn't know  why I was in prison did you were you  allowed to have a Bible eventually it  took a while before I could have any  books or Bible but eventually I did have  one is there a passage that got you  through all this  well I read second Timothy a lot where  Paul talks about suffering and finishing  the race well and this is became my  prayer I want to be faithful and endure  and finish well Noreen when you heard he  was getting out of prison how did you  all receive the news that it was over  incredibly relieved we got on our knees  Courthouse yeah didn't care what anybody  thought yeah and us to me three children  who called turkey home for so many years  I want to ask you about your experience  coming home and meeting with the  president in the Oval Office what  the first thing he said to you I think  he probably said welcome home and then  after that yeah I don't really remember  but we Noreen had actually had a dream  about praying for the president before  and so she had that in her heart  so before we went to the White House we  prayed together and said ask God to give  us opportunity to pray for the president  and we asked him if we could do it and  he said yes yes Noreen no so I had a  specific dream specific verses so when  there was the opportunity I knew exactly  what I was supposed to pray over him now  I know you all love turkey yeah in  Isaiah 11 you lived there for 23 years  what is your feeling about the country  now what are you thinking you know we  love the country we love it we love the  people we have dear friends there we  pray for its blessing but you're staying  here we're here for now I don't think we  can go back right now one of the most  hated people in Turkey so and definitely  forgiveness has to be a part of this we  don't have an option not to forgive as  Christians but it is something it's not  easy so we're working through that  there's a big community that's welcoming  you back here and glad that you're back  home thank you so much for joining you  thank you
 

